From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:52:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] tpm: Leave the self test to the TPM after starting it up

tpm2_auto_startup() sends TPM2_SelfTest with fullTest NO as its probe:
a TPM nothing has started refuses it with TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE, and the
kernel then sends TPM2_Startup and the self test again. Whichever of the
two self tests runs on a started TPM asks it to test every algorithm it
has not tested yet, which right after a startup is all of them, and the
probe waits for the answer.

A TPM tests an algorithm before its first use whether or not it was
asked to (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Self-Test Modes"), so the self test only
moves that work into the probe. Probe with TPM2_Startup instead, which
a TPM the firmware started refuses with TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE, and send no
self test. The startup's own response code still says whether the TPM
came up, and a TPM in failure mode is still found by
tpm2_get_cc_attrs_tbl(), whose TPM2_RC_FAILURE sets
TPM_CHIP_FLAG_FIRMWARE_UPGRADE as before. tpm2_do_selftest() has no
caller left and goes.

The self test is libtpms' longest command at boot: swtpm 0.10.2 took
25 ms to answer it on a laptop, and every other command of the probe
under 2 ms. In a nested KVM guest with tpm-crb, the probe slept 18.5 ms
on it before PID 1 that a machine without a TPM does not, whether the
kernel or the firmware started the TPM.

"tpm: Start the tpm2 before running a self test" (2023-11) met the same
unstarted TPM and kept both self tests; the answer was that firmware
should start the TPM. A firmware that does leaves the kernel's first
self test to pay instead.

Link: https://patchew.org/linux/20231122065528.1049819-1-hermin.anggawijaya@alliedtelesis.co.nz
Signed-off-by: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c | 62 ++++++-------------------------------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c b/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c
index 4b2bb2d..4e53e7b 100644
--- a/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c
@@ -412,45 +412,6 @@ void tpm2_shutdown(struct tpm_chip *chip, u16 shutdown_type)
 	tpm_transmit_cmd(chip, buf, 0, "stopping the TPM");
 }
 
-/**
- * tpm2_do_selftest() - ensure that all self tests have passed
- *
- * @chip: TPM chip to use
- *
- * Return: Same as with tpm_transmit_cmd.
- *
- * The TPM can either run all self tests synchronously and then return
- * RC_SUCCESS once all tests were successful. Or it can choose to run the tests
- * asynchronously and return RC_TESTING immediately while the self tests still
- * execute in the background. This function handles both cases and waits until
- * all tests have completed.
- */
-static int tpm2_do_selftest(struct tpm_chip *chip)
-{
-	int full;
-	int rc;
-
-	for (full = 0; full < 2; full++) {
-		struct tpm_buf *buf __free(kfree) = NULL;
-
-		buf = kzalloc(TPM_BUFSIZE, GFP_KERNEL);
-		if (!buf)
-			return -ENOMEM;
-
-		tpm_buf_init(buf, TPM_BUFSIZE);
-		tpm_buf_reset(buf, TPM2_ST_NO_SESSIONS, TPM2_CC_SELF_TEST);
-		tpm_buf_append_u8(buf, full);
-		rc = tpm_transmit_cmd(chip, buf, 0,
-				      "attempting the self test");
-		if (rc == TPM2_RC_TESTING)
-			rc = TPM2_RC_SUCCESS;
-		if (rc == TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE || rc == TPM2_RC_SUCCESS)
-			return rc;
-	}
-
-	return rc;
-}
-
 /**
  * tpm2_probe() - probe for the TPM 2.0 protocol
  * @chip:	a &tpm_chip instance
@@ -692,8 +653,6 @@ static int tpm2_startup(struct tpm_chip *chip)
 {
 	struct tpm_buf *buf __free(kfree) = NULL;
 
-	dev_info(&chip->dev, "starting up the TPM manually\n");
-
 	buf = kzalloc(TPM_BUFSIZE, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!buf)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -719,20 +678,17 @@ int tpm2_auto_startup(struct tpm_chip *chip)
 	if (rc)
 		goto out;
 
-	rc = tpm2_do_selftest(chip);
-	if (rc && rc != TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE)
+	/*
+	 * A TPM tests each algorithm before its first use, so a self test here
+	 * would only move that work into the probe. TPM2_Startup is refused
+	 * with TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE when the firmware has started the TPM.
+	 */
+	rc = tpm2_startup(chip);
+	if (!rc)
+		dev_info(&chip->dev, "started up the TPM\n");
+	else if (rc != TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE)
 		goto out;
 
-	if (rc == TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE) {
-		rc = tpm2_startup(chip);
-		if (rc)
-			goto out;
-
-		rc = tpm2_do_selftest(chip);
-		if (rc)
-			goto out;
-	}
-
 	rc = tpm2_get_cc_attrs_tbl(chip);
 	if (rc == TPM2_RC_FAILURE || (rc < 0 && rc != -ENOMEM)) {
 		dev_info(&chip->dev,
-- 
2.53.0

